Subject: [PATCH] DPP: send v2 Configuration Result before delivering credentials

Base: ESP-IDF v6.1, fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643
Date: 2026-10-16

Experimental patch; Pixel runtime validation pending.
Send an AES-SIV protected Configuration Result for a valid v2 configuration.
Defer the application event and legacy-AKM auth cleanup until matching TX_DONE,
so station connection cannot cancel the final DPP frame. Bound the asynchronous
wait and release pending credentials on failure, timeout, or teardown.
The v1 delivery path and public API are unchanged.

